  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1219 PM CDT Sun Aug 16 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge will move overhead by Tuesday morning bringing \nthe hottest temperatures of the week on Tuesday afternoon. \nTemperatures may again reach advisory criteria for areas off the \ncaprock for Tuesday. The ridge will continue drifting west settling \nnear the four corners region by Wednesday and remaining there for \nthe rest of the week afterwards. Mid and upper level flow will \ntransition to the northwest and potentially bring a brief period of \nnorthwest flow storms mid to late week. A short wave trough of \nvarying amplitude, depending on the model of choice, will swing \nacross the Central Plains sometime during the second half of the \nweek. This system will attempt to bring a cold front southward into \nthe Texas Panhandle but certainty is low in how far south this front \nwill move.",
